[ ] 74 Keypad node (PnKeypad) -- a pocket-calculator key pad in the
       node's client area. Ten digits, ".", the four basic operators, "=", "C"
       and "CE"; clicking a key emits one message naming the key. The node does
       no arithmetic and holds no accumulator: it is an input device, and the
       natural partner downstream is the Calculator (PnExpression) node that
       evaluates what the pad types.

       [x] 74.1 Core lib/pn-keypad.[ch] (GTK-free): the static 4x5 layout
             table published in the header, pn_keypad_key_rect_in() as the one
             shared placement call, pn_keypad_hit_key(), pn_keypad_press() /
             pn_keypad_press_code(), and the transient pressed-key highlight.
             Sources category, fa-keyboard-o (NOT the Calculator's
             fa-calculator), no input port.
       [x] 74.2 Message shape: data.key (ASCII code -- the operator keys paint
             the typographic signs but emit "*" "/" "-" so the code drops
             straight into an expression string), data.kind (digit / point /
             operator / equals / clear / clear-entry) and data.value on the
             digit keys ONLY. No startup announce -- a keypad has no state to
             report.
       [x] 74.3 GUI tier lib/pn-keypad-gui.[ch]: the cairo case + keys +
             legends, placing every key through the core's shared rect call so
